<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <Import Project="..\build\Package.props" />
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AssemblyName>LokiBulkDataProcessor.Core</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>LokiBulkDataProcessor.Core</PackageId>
    <RootNamespace>Loki.BulkDataProcessor</RootNamespace>
    <Title>Loki Bulk Data Processor Core</Title>
    <Description>Provider-neutral core of Loki Bulk Data Processor: the mapping API (ModelMapping, DataMapping), IBulkProcessor, IBulkProcessorFactory, the JSON reader, the shared bulk-copy pipeline and the provider SPI. Do not install it on its own; install a provider package such as LokiBulkDataProcessor (SQL Server), which depends on it.</Description>
    <PackageTags>loki bulk-copy bulk-insert etl datareader datatable json mapping</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes><![CDATA[
        9.0.0: new package, the provider-neutral core shared by LokiBulkDataProcessor (SQL Server) and LokiBulkDataProcessor.Oracle. It holds the types that used to live in LokiBulkDataProcessor (mapping API, IBulkProcessor, JSON reader, LokiLoggingOptions) with unchanged namespaces; LokiBulkDataProcessor forwards them here. New: IBulkProcessorFactory (a processor per provider and connection string), AddLokiBulkDataProcessor(options) with a provider builder, RequireDataMappingForJson and MaxJsonPayloadBytes, SaveAsync(IDataReader, destination, sourceName), SaveAsync(Stream, destinationTableName), an optional CancellationToken on every SaveAsync, and the public provider SPI (Loki.BulkDataProcessor.Providers). One shared pipeline for every input shape: settings are per processor instance (#11), a failed copy never rolls back the caller's transaction (#12), Loki's connection and transaction are disposed on failure (#13), errors have fixed, data-free messages with the driver exception as InnerException (#15), and DataMapping lookup follows one rule (#16). Behaviour changes: connection open/begin failures throw InvalidOperationException and a cancelled save throws OperationCanceledException, both with the driver exception as InnerException; mappings are validated at registration and duplicates fail at startup; AddLokiBulkDataProcessor may be called once; Transaction = null clears it; argument errors are thrown synchronously; get-only model properties are skipped instead of throwing NullReferenceException (#19); JSON booleans must be true/false, non-ISO dates use the invariant culture and conversion errors are data-free FormatExceptions; Loki logs through the host's ILoggerFactory by default (new category Loki.BulkDataProcessor.Internal.BulkProcessor) and console logging is obsolete. See the README Upgrade guide.
]]></PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FastMember" Version="1.5.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Console" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Providers use only the public SPI, so no provider assembly gets InternalsVisibleTo. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="LokiBulkDataProcessor.UnitTests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
